import{_ as a,C as r,o as n,c as o,j as e,a as i,E as h,a6 as d}from"./chunks/framework.CCKCzdWs.js";const v=JSON.parse(`{"title":"Share a run live","description":"Let a teammate watch the tests of a Playwright run on your machine from its page on the team instance, as a CI run's live view: Share live from VS Code, a JetBrains IDE, Piwi Picker's Runs window or the desktop app.","frontmatter":{"title":"Share a run live","description":"Let a teammate watch the tests of a Playwright run on your machine from its page on the team instance, as a CI run's live view: Share live from VS Code, a JetBrains IDE, Piwi Picker's Runs window or the desktop app.","lang":"en-US","head":[["link",{"rel":"canonical","href":"https://piwitests.dev/features/share-live.html"}],["meta",{"property":"og:url","content":"https://piwitests.dev/features/share-live.html"}],["meta",{"property":"og:title","content":"Share a run live | Piwi for Playwright"}],["meta",{"property":"og:description","content":"Let a teammate watch the tests of a Playwright run on your machine from its page on the team instance, as a CI run's live view: Share live from VS Code, a JetBrains IDE, Piwi Picker's Runs window or the desktop app."}]]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"features/share-live.md","filePath":"features/share-live.md","lastUpdated":1794492047000}`),l={name:"features/share-live.md"};function p(u,t,g,c,w,m){const s=r("Needs");return n(),o("div",null,[t[0]||(t[0]=e("h1",{id:"share-a-run-live",tabindex:"-1"},[i("Share a run live "),e("a",{class:"header-anchor",href:"#share-a-run-live","aria-label":'Permalink to "Share a run live"'},"​")],-1)),h(s,{reporter:"",fixtures:""}),t[1]||(t[1]=d('<p>A run on your machine sends the team instance nothing of its pages until you share it. Shared, it gets the <a href="./live-view.html">live view</a> a CI run gets: a teammate opens its page and watches each worker, and its stops show on its rows. Sharing changes nothing for the run itself, and stops as you choose, or as the tool that shared it closes.</p><h2 id="share-and-stop" tabindex="-1">Share and stop <a class="header-anchor" href="#share-and-stop" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Share and stop&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Choose <strong>Share live</strong> while a local run executes to let a teammate watch it. The run must report to a team instance whose project enables live view, and connect to an editor or the desktop app for controls.</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Where</th><th>Share</th><th>Stop</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>VS Code</td><td><strong>Piwi: Share the run live on the team instance</strong>, or the status bar&#39;s broadcast icon</td><td><strong>Piwi: Stop sharing the run live</strong>, or the status bar&#39;s <strong>Live</strong></td></tr><tr><td>JetBrains IDEs</td><td><strong>Tools → Piwi → Share the Run Live</strong></td><td><strong>Tools → Piwi → Stop Sharing the Run Live</strong></td></tr><tr><td>Piwi Picker&#39;s <a href="./runs-window.html">Runs window</a></td><td><strong>Share live</strong> under the run&#39;s name</td><td><strong>Stop sharing</strong></td></tr><tr><td>The desktop app&#39;s <a href="./desktop-runs.html">Local runs tray</a></td><td><strong>Share live</strong> above the run&#39;s workers</td><td><strong>Stop sharing</strong></td></tr></tbody></table><p>The first share asks for confirmation; in an editor, it also asks whether to share this run or <a href="#a-window-s-runs">the window&#39;s runs</a>. The shared run shows its destination, viewer count and a link to copy.</p><p>Until then, its workers send nothing, and the run&#39;s <strong>Tests</strong> tab says <strong>Not shared live</strong> once, beside its search, with <a href="#ask-to-watch"><strong>Ask to watch</strong></a> for a teammate who may ask; its running tests say where they <a href="#stops-shared-or-not">stopped</a>. Once shared, images go only to those watching. <strong>Stop sharing</strong> closes the views within seconds. Closing the editor or the desktop app stops it too.</p><p>A run that cannot be shared says why: it reports to no instance or to the desktop app, it does not stream its results, its project has the live view off, the reporter&#39;s global setup did not register it, or the instance did not register the run as it started. A sharing that stops on its own says why (the live view turned off, or the instance stopped answering), and <strong>Share live</strong> shows again: shared again, the run streams once the instance answers with its live view on, a restarted instance taking the run&#39;s key back. A run the instance no longer holds live cannot be shared again.</p><h3 id="from-a-terminal" tabindex="-1">From a terminal <a class="header-anchor" href="#from-a-terminal" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;From a terminal&quot;">​</a></h3><p>A run you start in a terminal that no editor or app follows has no <strong>Share live</strong> to choose: set <code>PIWI_SHARE_LIVE=1</code> to share it from its start. The reporter prints what goes out and where before any image does, or why the run cannot be shared. A tool that follows the run can still stop it.</p><div class="vp-code-group vp-adaptive-theme"><div class="tabs"><input type="radio" name="group-DLzE5" id="tab-fgh4CAv" checked><label data-title="Linux / macOS" for="tab-fgh4CAv">Linux / macOS</label><input type="radio" name="group-DLzE5" id="tab-PVnuxdY"><label data-title="Windows (PowerShell)" for="tab-PVnuxdY">Windows (PowerShell)</label></div><div class="blocks"><div class="language-bash vp-adaptive-theme active"><button title="Copy Code" class="copy"></button><span class="lang">bash</span><pre class="shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark vp-code" tabindex="0"><code><span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">PIWI_SHARE_LIVE</span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">=</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;">1</span><span style="--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0;"> npx</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;"> playwright</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;"> test</span></span></code></pre></div><div class="language-powershell vp-adaptive-theme"><button title="Copy Code" class="copy"></button><span class="lang">powershell</span><pre class="shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark vp-code" tabindex="0"><code><span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">$</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;">env:</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">PIWI_SHARE_LIVE</span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">=</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;">&#39;1&#39;</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">; npx playwright test</span></span></code></pre></div></div></div><h3 id="a-window-s-runs" tabindex="-1">A window&#39;s runs <a class="header-anchor" href="#a-window-s-runs" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;A window&#39;s runs&quot;">​</a></h3><p><strong>Piwi: Share this window&#39;s runs live until I stop</strong> in VS Code, and <strong>Tools → Piwi → Share This Project&#39;s Runs Live Until I Stop</strong> in a JetBrains IDE, share each run the window starts from then on, each one said as it is shared, until you stop (<strong>…Stop sharing this window&#39;s runs live</strong>, or a click on the status bar&#39;s <strong>Live · this window</strong>) or close the window. On the team instance, the page of the run before says <strong>Continued in run #78</strong>, linked, and a teammate who has it open is taken to the new run, on the worker they were watching.</p><h2 id="ask-to-watch" tabindex="-1">Ask to watch <a class="header-anchor" href="#ask-to-watch" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Ask to watch&quot;">​</a></h2><p>A teammate who opens a running run of yours that is not shared can ask you to share it: <strong>Ask to watch</strong>, beside <strong>Not shared live</strong>. The tool you launched the run from asks you, naming the person who asks, and offers <strong>Share live</strong> and <strong>Not now</strong>; a run that no tool follows prints the ask in its terminal. Their page shows your answer: <strong>Asked to watch</strong> while it waits, <strong>The developer answered Not now</strong>, or the live view once you share.</p><ul><li><strong>Who</strong> — anyone signed in who may open the run. With sign-in off on the instance, nobody is named, and asking is not offered.</li><li><strong>How often</strong> — one ask per person and run every 5 minutes; their page says when they may ask again.</li><li><strong>Which runs</strong> — a running run from a developer&#39;s machine that holds a live view key, never a CI run, whose workers stream as they start.</li><li><strong>Turn it off</strong> — a Project admin turns off <strong>Let signed-in readers ask to watch a run nobody shares</strong> in the project&#39;s <strong>Live view</strong> settings; it is on by default. Turning it off, or the live view, drops the asks that wait.</li></ul><p>Asks are kept in the instance&#39;s memory, never stored, and end with the run.</p><h2 id="stops-shared-or-not" tabindex="-1">Stops, shared or not <a class="header-anchor" href="#stops-shared-or-not" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Stops, shared or not&quot;">​</a></h2><p>A test of a run on your machine stops at a breakpoint, a <code>page.pause()</code>, a step or <strong>Run to here</strong>, and its row on the run&#39;s page says why, at the stopped call: <strong>Stopped at a breakpoint</strong>, <strong>Stopped at page.pause()</strong>, <strong>Paused</strong>. The call&#39;s place opens in your editor. A shared run&#39;s row tells it from its live view. A run nobody shares tells it as text, with <code>@piwitests/reporter</code> 0.68.0 or later, and says for how long once the stop has stood a minute: its results stream sends the call&#39;s title, its file and line, the test&#39;s title and since when, as each stop shows and ends. Never an image. A test that stands stopped is never marked <a href="./stuck-tests.html"><strong>Stuck?</strong></a>.</p><h2 id="from-the-desktop-app" tabindex="-1">From the desktop app <a class="header-anchor" href="#from-the-desktop-app" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;From the desktop app&quot;">​</a></h2><p>A run that reports to the <a href="./desktop-runs.html">desktop app</a> itself (a reproduction, a bisect, a <strong>Re-run</strong> in a folder that names no instance, a run your editor started) cannot be shared: the app hands out no live view key, since no teammate reaches it. Its tray offers no <strong>Share live</strong> for it, the app&#39;s project settings have no <strong>Live view</strong> section, and on the run&#39;s page its running tests offer <a href="./desktop-runs.html#watch-live"><strong>Watch</strong> and <strong>Pause and watch</strong></a>, shown in the app&#39;s tray from the app itself. A run your editor started says <strong>See its page at a stop</strong> there: its page shows where the editor steers it.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><a href="./live-view.html">Live view of a run</a>: what a teammate sees, what is sent and what is kept</li><li><a href="./editor-run-control.html">Editor run control</a>: the controls of a run your editor starts</li><li><a href="./runs-window.html">Runs window</a>: Piwi Picker&#39;s view of your runs</li><li><a href="./desktop-runs.html">Desktop app runs</a>: the desktop app&#39;s runs and its tray</li></ul>',22))])}const f=a(l,[["render",p]]);export{v as __pageData,f as default};
